    "available_at": "2026-11-28T03:39:14.546503+00:00",
    "body": "Great on any Friday: WOLFBOX MV24 4000A - Car Jump Starter with 65W Quick Charger\nBMW's First Large Minivan Wants a Piece of the North American Sliding-Door MPV Sector – Rendering\n7 photos\nPhoto: kelsonik / Instagram\nThe Bavarian automaker BMW just kicked off production of its first-ever US-made all-electric model – Plant Spartanburg and the Woodruff nearby location now make the US’s first electric SUV from BMW, all thanks to a $1.7 billion investment to make the all-new, first-ever BMW iX5 feel right at home in North America.\nThe largest premium automaker in the world dares to take a leap of faith at a time when the US automotive market isn’t in love with EVs anymore but with hybrids. Alas, they probably don’t worry much, as the iX5 will be shipped all around the world, plus they have a long list of novelties coming out next year to make sure they cover all customer needs.\nThere’s a new BMW i1 coming as the entry-level EV , fresh X1 and iX1 subcompact crossover SUVs, updated X2 and iX2 models, the practical i3 Touring, the first-ever all-electric M3 plus an iX3 M along with an iX4 M, and also the major Neue Klasse redesign of the 5 Series and M5, plus the upcoming all-new X7 and iX7 along with the BMW Alpina 7 flagships .\nQuite obviously, there will be something for everyone – both ICE and EV along with PHEV in between them. Alas, there’s one person who thinks that BMW still has room for one more new vehicle in the roster. He’s a member of the imaginative guild of digital car content creators, and he stopped dwelling across the parallel universes of vehicular CGI for this – their latest unofficial, hypothetical design project.\nNikita Chuicko, the virtual artist better known as \" kelsonik \" on social media, thinks that now is the right CGI time to work on something different for BMW – a large Neue Klasse minivan. This model could attack the large Mercedes-Benz MPV, the all-new and all-electric VLE – which is the primary target from the standpoint of the pixel master.\nAs such, it would provide an exotic alternative to the VLE , which features two powertrain versions – a front-motor FWD version, VLE 300, and the dual-motor AWD VLE 400 4Matic, packing 271 or 415 hp and a 115-kWh battery pack on an 800-volt architecture with up to 678 km (421 miles) of range. The rivaling BMW minivan could share the fresh Neue Klasse architecture with the i3 and iX3, rocking their RWD and dual-motor AWD powertrains with up to 463 horsepower and comparable range.\nBut on the other hand, we’d really like this quirky minivan to also come to North America, where it could provide an interesting alternative to the likes of Chrysler Pacifica, Toyota Sienna, Honda Odyssey, and the Kia Carnival. It would need an ICE or hybrid powertrain, though, as Americans aren’t fond of EVs too much these days. Cool or not? View this post on Instagram A post shared by CAR DESIGN | RENDERINGS (@kelsonik)\nLiked the article? Follow us to see more stories from autoevolution in your Google feeds.\nBMW Neue Klasse MPV BMW Neue Klasse MPV Mercedes-Benz VLE CGI minivan rendering kelsonik\nAbout the author: Aurel Niculescu\nAurel has aimed high all his life (literally, at 16 he was flying gliders all by himself) so in 2006 he switched careers and got hired as a writer at his favorite magazine. Since then, his work has been published both by print and online outlets, most recently right here, on autoevolution. Full profile\nUP NEXT Virtually Reborn Ford Thunderbird Super Coupe Steals the CGI Soul of a Mighty Aston Martin Valen",
